From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: the MLD must not overwrite a counted num_sta

993 and 999994 both aimed at the same field and both left the count wrong on
hardware. 999994 was verified on 2026-08-27 with the image deployed to all
four nodes: an agent with two clients on its radio reported one, another with
two reported none.

The arithmetic in agent.c was never the problem. mld_parse_affiliated_ap()
assigned ap->num_sta unconditionally from the MLD status object, and it runs
after agent.c has done its work. Every AP affiliated with a fronthaul MLD -
which is all of them - therefore had its counted value replaced by whatever
the MLD reported, and the MLD reports zero for the same reason the per-AP
object does:

	iw dev ap-mld-1 station dump      2 stations
	ubus wifi.ap.ap-mld-1 stations    2 entries, correct MACs
	ubus wifi.ap.ap-mld-1 status      "num_stations": 0
	ubus wifi.apmld.ap-mld-1 status   "num_stations": 0, three times
	ubus map.agent status             num_sta 1 on one node, 0 on the other

Apply the same rule agent.c already uses: believe a non-zero count, and when
the MLD says none while stations are still held, count them. A real
last-client-leaves empties the list too, so a genuine zero still lands.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/mld.c
+++ b/src/mld.c
@@ -325,8 +325,46 @@
 	if (tb[9])
 		strncpy(ap->standard, blobmsg_data(tb[9]), sizeof(ap->standard) - 1);
 
-	if (tb[10])
-		ap->num_sta = blobmsg_get_u32(tb[10]);
+	if (tb[10]) {
+		uint32_t mld_num_sta = blobmsg_get_u32(tb[10]);
+
+		/* Do not undo a count that was worked out from the list.
+		 *
+		 * This assignment used to be unconditional, and it runs after
+		 * the guard in parse_ap_status()/agent.c, so it had the last
+		 * word on ap->num_sta for every AP affiliated with an MLD -
+		 * which, on a fronthaul MLD, is all of them. Measured
+		 * 2026-08-27 on two agents, each serving two clients, well
+		 * after boot:
+		 *
+		 *   iw dev ap-mld-1 station dump      2 stations
+		 *   ubus wifi.ap.ap-mld-1 stations    2 entries, correct MACs
+		 *   ubus wifi.ap.ap-mld-1 status      "num_stations": 0
+		 *   ubus wifi.apmld.ap-mld-1 status   "num_stations": 0 (x3)
+		 *   ubus map.agent status             num_sta 1 and 0
+		 *
+		 * The MLD object reports zero for the same reason the per-AP
+		 * object does, and this line copied that zero over a figure
+		 * agent.c had just counted correctly. That is why 993 and
+		 * 999994 both looked almost right and never matched: they fixed
+		 * the arithmetic but were not the last writer.
+		 *
+		 * Same rule as agent.c: believe a non-zero count, and when the
+		 * MLD says none while we are still holding stations, count them
+		 * instead. A genuine last-client-leaves empties stalist too, so
+		 * a real zero still lands. */
+		if (mld_num_sta > 0 || list_empty(&ap->stalist)) {
+			ap->num_sta = mld_num_sta;
+		} else {
+			struct sta *s;
+			uint32_t n = 0;
+
+			list_for_each_entry(s, &ap->stalist, list)
+				n++;
+
+			ap->num_sta = n;
+		}
+	}
 
 	ap->enabled = tb[17] ? blobmsg_get_bool(tb[17]) : false;
 
